/**
 * The grammar ISO/IEC 39075 specifies, read from ISO's own artifact.
 *
 * The artifact's header says it is published so that implementers can generate parsers
 * for GQL from it, which makes it the one place a claim about GQL's syntax can be
 * settled without a reader having to take an implementer's word for anything.
 *
 * Only the two productions that decide what a name may be are read here. They are the
 * ones an implementation is tempted to skip, because skipping them costs nothing until
 * a query that means one thing in GQL means another in the implementation.
 *
 * @see spec/iso/README.md Where the artifact comes from and how to verify it
 */
